 "remarks": "A ready canvas for the next generation of visionary homeowners and craftsmen. Flat, easily buildable, screened on every side: the kind of land and location Westport buyers are chasing hardest right now, and finding least. Long Lots, on the cusp of Hunt Club - the neighborhood and the country club. Close to town but not too close. A quick drive to Greens Farms station, Burying Hill Beach, and the many Post Road amenities - dangerously close to Fatto a Mano, though proximity to Equinox balances that right out. Zone Specifics: AA Zone, 30 ft from the street and 25 ft from the side setbacks, max 3 stories height of 40 ft, 25% coverage. No wetlands. Public water, septic. Access to both Gregg Lane and Grist Mill. In the supplements: original survey, existing septic map, GIS map, tank removal info. Existing solar will be removed and settled by the trust. Buyers are responsible for their own due diligence; neither the trust nor the seller's agent can make any representations. The address is 4 Grist Mill Lane, the driveway is at the end of Gregg Lane. As-is. Not subject to probate approval.",
